From c6c658db94ac0757546157e1bab0711af44eb6d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:57:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(verify): judge a stock-sourced Bore's entry rapid against
 the stock

The planar ladder rapids to the top of the cut plus the plunge height;
for Bore that top is the hole's mouth. Under a block standing higher
than the mouth the rapid ends in uncut stock. Pocket, Contour and a
part-sourced Bore were already convicted by the rapid law (#96), but a
Bore whose source is the stock posted silently: the column law read
"is this stock?" from the op's region, which for Bore and Thread is
the stock footprint with the holes' rims punched out.

material_source::judged_stock hands the verify (upright and 3+2) the
stock's own facets for a stock-sourced Bore or Thread; every other
source and kind reads as before. Pinned by ladder_entry_height.rs over
Pocket, Bore and Contour: convicted and blocked 5 mm under the block,
silent inside the plunge height and with stock to the mouth, acquitted
by a face ahead.

Fixes #1066

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
